Package: pnp
Version: @DEB_VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: RegulusArms <ross@regulusarms.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: libc6 (>= @GLIBC@), passwd
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://pnp.regulusarms.com
Description: one-time pad file encryption that stays secure even if P = NP
 pnp encrypts any file with a one-time pad: a key of random bytes as long as
 the file, read from the machine's hardware random number generators
 (/dev/hwrng and the CPU's RDSEED instruction), health-checked as they're
 read, and combined with XOR. A one-time pad's security doesn't rest on any
 problem being hard to compute, so it holds even if P = NP.
 .
 pnp FILE writes FILE.pnp and its key FILE.pnp.key; pnp -d FILE.pnp
 decrypts it; pnp alone opens an interactive file browser that shows what
 will be written, and which key on the key drive will be used. Keys can be
 split into shares, and optionally locked with a passphrase (a
 computationally secure extra, not part of the P = NP claim).
 Members of the pnp group may read /dev/hwrng.
